d pair up to form hydrogen gas. Since gas is lighter than liquid, it forms tiny bubbles that fizz and rise to the surface, escaping into the air.\",\n    \"background\": \"default\",\n    \"atoms\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"fe1\",\n        \"element\": \"Fe\",\n        \"x\": 1.8,\n        \"y\": 0,\n        \"z\": 0\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"cl1\",\n        \"element\": \"Cl\",\n        \"x\": 0.5,\n        \"y\": 0,\n        \"z\": 0\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"cl2\",\n        \"element\": \"Cl\",\n        \"x\": 3.1,\n        \"y\": 0,\n        \"z\": 0\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"h1\",\n        \"element\": \"H\",\n        \"x\": -2,\n        \"y\": 0,\n        \"z\": 0\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"h2\",\n        \"element\": \"H\",\n        \"x\": -1.5,\n        \"y\": 0,\n        \"z\": 0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"bonds\": [\n      {\n        \"from\": \"cl1\",\n        \"to\": \"fe1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"cl2\",\n        \"to\": \"fe1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"h1\",\n        \"to\": \"h2\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"electronTransfers\": [],\n    \"atomOverrides\": {\n      \"fe1\": {\n        \"radiusScale\": 0.8,\n        \"dimmed\": true\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]");

